=== HYPOTHESIS ===
# p_4f7a — Guitar on the Couch by Day, Bedroom Floor 18–21 (fork of p_8c3d)

The parent (p_8c3d) placed the guitar on the bedroom floor as its default resting spot and on the couch only after 22:00. The sightings refute this: from 00:00 through 16:00 the pass finds guitar_yuki on `couch_l1` twice and on `bedroom_floor_b1` once, making the couch the clear daytime home. At 18:00 and 20:00 the pattern flips — `bedroom_floor_b1` appears twice and `couch_l1` once — indicating Yuki brings the guitar to the bedroom for her evening practice session. By 22:00 it is back on the couch (2-to-1). The mixture's worst-object list confirms: "predicted couch_l1, actually bedroom_floor_b1 — 6x, e.g. day 2 18:00" means the *other* documents (which put it on the couch all day) are wrong at 18:00, but p_8c3d is wrong the other way (it predicts bedroom floor at 14:00 when the couch is correct).

What changed from the parent: the default block for guitar_yuki is now `couch_l1` (was `bedroom_floor_b1`). The bedroom-floor window is 17:00–21:00 (was no bedroom-floor block; the parent only had a couch block at 22:00+). The post-21:00 couch block is retained. The dog food bag and dog bowl blocks are unchanged from the parent.

What sets this apart: between 14:00 and 17:00 on a weekday, the guitar is on the couch (not the bedroom floor as p_8c3d claims). Between 18:00 and 21:00 it is on the bedroom floor (Yuki's practice). After 21:00 it returns to the couch.

What would refute it: finding the guitar on the bedroom floor at 14:00 or 16:00 on a weekday, or finding it on the couch at 19:00 on a weekday.

